# Fleet inventory — real addresses live in .env, which is gitignored.
# Copy this file and fill it in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# This repo is public, so validator addresses, per-host maintenance windows and
# the peer list are deliberately kept out of it. Anything an operator tool needs
# at runtime is read from the local copy instead of being hardcoded.
#
# Every value is optional. Tools that need one and cannot find it fail with a
# message naming the key, rather than silently falling back to a wrong host.

# Hosts the fleet-wide operator tools act on, in the order they should be
# visited. Comma-separated; each entry is a hostname or an IP, without a user
# prefix (the tools add their own).
MIRAGE_FLEET_HOSTS=

# CometBFT RPC endpoint used when submitting governance proposals from a
# workstation. Use a direct address: the public hostnames sit behind a CDN that
# does not proxy port 26657.
MIRAGE_REMOTE_RPC=

# Persistent peers for a freshly initialised node, comma-separated as
# node_id@host:26656. Existing nodes keep whatever is already in their
# ~/.mirage/env/node.env — the template only seeds new installs.
# Generate with scripts/get_persistent_peers.sh.
MIRAGE_PERSISTENT_PEERS=

# Maintenance windows, as a note to the operator — nothing reads these. They
# live here rather than in the docs so the repo does not advertise when any
# given validator is down. Record which host holds which slot, e.g.
#   MIRAGE_WEEKLY_RESTART_SLOTS=val4 Mon 08, val3 Mon 09, ...
# Rules that do belong in the docs, and are documented there: one host per
# hour, never two at once, and clear of both the backup sweep and the per-host
# OS upgrade slot.
MIRAGE_WEEKLY_RESTART_SLOTS=
MIRAGE_WEEKLY_UPGRADE_SLOTS=
MIRAGE_BACKUP_WINDOW=
